  "id": "Compound::DB00718 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Adefovir Dipivoxil is implicated in the pathogenesis of Fanconi Syndrome and Renal Tubular Disorder through a shared mechanism involving Tenofovir and Cidofovir, both of which are nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs). These agents bind to Slc22a6, a transporter protein involved in the reabsorption of nucleosides in the renal tubules. The observed relationship between Adefovir Dipivoxil and Slc22a6 is mediated through the indirect pathway involving NRTIs, suggesting a potential role for Slc22a6 in the renal toxicity associated with these drugs. The evidence is consistent with a dependency on Slc22a6 for the retention of nucleosides, which may be disrupted by the binding of these agents, leading to renal dysfunction. The integration of these paths highlights a recurring mechanism where NRTIs, through their interaction with Slc22a6, contribute to the development of renal disorders, underscoring the importance of this transporter in drug-induced nephrotoxicity.",
